WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.700
Hey, Thoughty 2 here.
 
Jesus Christ, Nelson Mandela and Adolf Hitler;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.820
aside from being costumes guaranteed to cause&nbsp;
a stir at a fancy dress party, these historical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:16.560
heavyweights all have something in common.
 
They were all leaders of such passion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:22.560
conviction and charisma, that they could compel&nbsp;
their followers to do things, both good and evil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:29.040
they would otherwise never have considered.
 
Today’s story of madness, mock messiahs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:34.440
and mass murder focuses on someone who&nbsp;
combined elements of all three. He was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:40.200
captivating preacher with the gift of the gab, a&nbsp;
firebrand political leader who advocated radical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.640
socialism and racial harmony, and a tyrant who&nbsp;
used violence and death to achieve his aims.
 &nbsp;

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.500
Rising to prominence during the era of&nbsp;
peace and love he eventually declared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.600
himself to be the Messiah, but instead&nbsp;
turned out to be a very naughty boy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:03.960
After brainwashing his thousands of followers&nbsp;
into giving up their money and freedom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.840
he eventually cost them their lives&nbsp;
by engineering what is to this day the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:16.320
largest mass suicide in modern history.
 
This is the twisted tale of Jim Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:23.280
a self-styled prophet who mixed spirituality with&nbsp;
criminality and convinced his congregation he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:29.100
would give them heaven on earth, but instead&nbsp;
brought about his own personal apocalypse.
 
 &nbsp;

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:10.380
Jones was born into abject misery&nbsp;
in rural Indiana in May 1931.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.520
His father had been crippled in World&nbsp;
War One and struggled to find work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:21.900
and his mother had all the maternal instincts of a&nbsp;
frog with amnesia. The family were evicted during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:27.960
the Great Depression of the 1930s, relocating into&nbsp;
what was little more than a shack with no indoor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:33.120
plumbing or electricity. Things got so bad they&nbsp;
were forced to forage for food in nearby fields.
 &nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.860
Jim was left to his own devices from a&nbsp;
very young age, he frequently toddled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:42.060
through town naked as an infant because&nbsp;
there was no one around to dress him. 
 &nbsp;

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:46.140
At some point in his childhood, he was&nbsp;
given a Bible by the wife of a local pastor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:53.880
and it turned out to be a lightning bolt moment&nbsp;
for the oft-nude infant. He studied the book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:59.940
ceaselessly and began to attend multiple churches&nbsp;
every week, getting baptised in several of them. 
 &nbsp;

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:06.420
Religion and death fascinated Jones even&nbsp;
then; he gave sermons to the local kids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:12.720
and held mock funerals for roadkill. He also&nbsp;
claimed to have special powers, on one occasion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:19.020
swearing blind he could fly - a boast that was&nbsp;
proven a lie shortly afterwards when he jumped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:23.580
off a roof and broke his arm. 
 
When he wasn’t reading the Bible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:28.440
Jones was engrossed in works by the&nbsp;
likes of Stalin, Mao, and Gandhi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:34.080
If it isn’t obvious already, he was far from your&nbsp;
average kid. Instead of comic books and candy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:40.380
it was more… communism and cat funerals.
 
When World War Two broke out, Jones’ new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:45.720
Nazi fascination surprised no one. He&nbsp;
commanded the neighbourhood children to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:50.460
goose-step in time with him on pretend&nbsp;
marches and beat them if they refused.
 &nbsp;

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:57.060
Between the roadkill funerals and the enforced&nbsp;
fascism Jones had done little to endear himself to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:04.200
his school friends and this pattern persisted into&nbsp;
puberty. He went full-briefcase wanker by wearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.460
his Sunday church clothes to School and always&nbsp;
carried a Bible, regularly lecturing his fellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:16.980
students about the dangers of the 3 Ds - drinking,&nbsp;
dancing, and the biggest D of all - the devil.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:24.420
Unless your idea of a good time was linking arms&nbsp;
and reading Psalms, Jim Jones was definitely not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:29.220
the guy to get stuck with at a house party.
 
 
At college, he became increasingly politically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:34.320
active and started attending Communist Party&nbsp;
meetings. This was America in the ‘50s and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:39.720
the Red Scare was in full effect; merely being&nbsp;
suspected of sympathising with the Communists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:44.580
could get you blacklisted by the government.
 
Considering that Jones and his young wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:51.180
Marceline actually were commies, it’s no&nbsp;
surprise they were regularly harassed by the FBI.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.860 --> 00:06:01.020
But these ideological intrusions only served&nbsp;
to further radicalise the young couple.
 &nbsp;

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:06.960
In the early 50s, Jones worked as a pastor at&nbsp;
several churches across Indianapolis, and in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:14.220
1955 he founded the now-infamous People’s Temple&nbsp;
- it was supposed to be a new religious movement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:20.700
that combined Christianity with communism, but&nbsp;
as we’ll soon discover, it rapidly devolved into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:25.980
one of history’s deadliest doomsday cults. 
 
To gain more followers in those early years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:30.480
Jones organised faith healing conventions during&nbsp;
which he would call upon the big man upstairs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.800
to do a spot of divine doctoring,&nbsp;
healing various ailments among the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:41.220
attendees. It worked too - not the healing,&nbsp;
obviously - the getting more followers bit.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:50.340
Despite his earlier admiration for a certain&nbsp;
tiny-moustached German, Jones went on to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:56.100
an advocate for racial harmony, and in 1960 the&nbsp;
Mayor of Indianapolis made him director of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:00.360
local human rights commission. For all the evil&nbsp;
that was to come later in Jones’ life, he actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:05.640
did a lot of good in the role. This was still&nbsp;
a time of stark division, with one set of rules&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:11.520
for the city’s white residents, and another for&nbsp;
everyone else. Jones worked tirelessly to break&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:17.820
down those barriers, desegregating everything&nbsp;
from the police department to the phone company.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:23.100
Jim’s desire for a more tolerant world&nbsp;
was evident in his personal life too;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:28.980
he and Marceline adopted six children&nbsp;
of various ethnicities to create what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:36.120
he questionably called his ‘rainbow family.’
 
But while outwardly he appeared to be a paragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:43.320
of virtue, Jones was growing increasingly&nbsp;
paranoid. In 1961 he told his congregation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:47.580
he’d had visions that a nuclear strike&nbsp;
would soon destroy Indianapolis.
 &nbsp;

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:55.620
Convinced America’s end was nigh, Jones&nbsp;
travelled to Brazil in 1962 to search&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.620 --> 00:08:00.420
for a new home for the People's Temple.
 
He settled in Rio de Janeiro, working in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:06.300
the city’s slums, but the Brazilian break didn’t&nbsp;
last long. Jones was unable to find a suitable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:11.760
HQ for his fledgling cult, and back home in&nbsp;
Indianapolis, which against all odds hadn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:17.220
been wiped off the map in a hail of nukes,&nbsp;
Jones’ fickle followers were drifting away.
 &nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:24.720
Diminished attendance brought financial issues,&nbsp;
and Jones was forced to sell several of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:32.700
People’s Temple assets, including the actual&nbsp;
temple. Awkward. In 1965 he left Indianapolis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:38.460
behind for good, moving his family and remaining&nbsp;
flock to Redwood Valley in California.
 &nbsp;

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:44.760
Once settled in The Golden State, things started&nbsp;
to get very dark very quickly. Jones continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:51.660
to preach that the apocalypse was coming but now&nbsp;
claimed to be the messiah sent to save the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:59.700
Despite fancying himself a divine incarnation,&nbsp;
his actions said otherwise; he began taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:06.720
copious amounts of drugs, and his control over&nbsp;
his remaining followers grew far more oppressive.
 &nbsp;

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:12.480
New members of the People’s Temple were forced&nbsp;
to transfer all their assets to the church, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:18.540
those who held day jobs gave their entire salaries&nbsp;
to their new God. Jones controlled every aspect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:25.140
of their lives - he set food rations, approved&nbsp;
sexual partners, and determined who could marry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:32.400
As for his own ‘needs’ - he took what he&nbsp;
wanted, even if what he wanted happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:39.720
to be married to another member of the Temple.&nbsp;
Jones set up an armed security unit to enforce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:45.360
his will and those who went against him were&nbsp;
subjected to increasingly severe punishments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:50.340
including reduced food rations, public&nbsp;
humiliation, and physical violence. 
 &nbsp;

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:59.100
As horrifying as this was, Jone had only just&nbsp;
begun. But no matter how outrageously he behaved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:05.580
privately, in public, his stardom continued to&nbsp;
rise. This was the age of the hippie, a time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:12.120
of making love not war and as the smell of joss&nbsp;
sticks floated across California, Jones’ message&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:19.200
of socialism and equality struck a chord. 
 
By 1970 the People’s Temple had opened a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:24.120
branch in L.A. and moved their headquarters&nbsp;
to the flower-power capital of the west coast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:30.240
San Francisco. Membership grew steadily&nbsp;
and Jones and his disciples would brazenly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:35.280
seek new recruits from rival churches.
 
Involvement in San Francisco politics allowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:40.680
Jones to befriend numerous city politicians, and&nbsp;
he courted the press, using an extensive network&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:45.840
of contacts to guarantee good publicity&nbsp;
for him and his cult... I mean church.
 &nbsp;

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:51.900
Despite the PR offensive, word was beginning to&nbsp;
get out that the People’s Temple wasn’t quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:57.240
the centre of virtue it seemed. As rumours&nbsp;
of exploitation and abuse began to spread,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:02.880
Jones decided it was probably a good idea&nbsp;
to move his flock far away from the eyes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:08.820
the media and beyond the reach of the police.
 
His destination of choice was, of all places,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:14.040
Guyana. The former British colony had a&nbsp;
recently-installed socialist government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:18.900
and for Jones, it was the perfect place&nbsp;
to reshape the world in his image.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:26.700
You might think convincing a bunch of Americans to&nbsp;
up sticks and relocate to the jungle to be ruled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:33.000
over by an abusive megalomaniac would be a hard&nbsp;
sell, but people do some pretty weird things when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:39.360
they believe their immortal soul is at stake. All&nbsp;
told, around a thousand faithful made the move.
 
 &nbsp;

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:46.620
Cult-based colonies don’t build themselves even if&nbsp;
they are founded by the actual messiah, so Jones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:53.160
soon put his loyal disciples to work toiling in&nbsp;
the fields twelve hours a day, six days a week.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:59.520
As a reward for all this hard labour,&nbsp;
the people of Jonestown were given food&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:03.960
rations that would have had your average&nbsp;
supermodel reaching for the snack drawer..
 &nbsp;

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:09.300
Nobody was allowed to leave and anyone who&nbsp;
spoke out about the appalling conditions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:13.980
would be sent to the ‘medical unit,’&nbsp;
where they were dosed with mind-altering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:20.700
drugs transforming them into walking zombies.
 
Jones himself continued to pop a plethora of pills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:27.000
and potions, all of which made his paranoia soar&nbsp;
to new heights. He was convinced that numerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:33.480
enemies were out to destroy the church, so along&nbsp;
with their back-breaking manual labour and lack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:38.220
of food, the People’s Temple congregation&nbsp;
were subjected to military-style drills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:44.160
including simulated attacks on the community.
 
Guards hidden in the forest would fire on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:49.920
commune whilst Jones chanted nonsense over&nbsp;
loudspeakers dotted around the place while his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:55.380
terrified followers took up weapons and stood&nbsp;
ready to repel their fictitious invaders.
 
 &nbsp;

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:02.160
By November of 1978 abuse in Jonestown had&nbsp;
become so widespread that the U.S. government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:09.000
sent a team led by California Congressman Leo&nbsp;
Ryan to investigate. The delegation included&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:15.720
newspaper reporters, a TV crew and relatives&nbsp;
of some Jonestown inmates - I mean residents.
 &nbsp;

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:23.760
Jones took the intrusion in his stride, holding a&nbsp;
small party for the outsiders. However, the facade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:30.780
of normalcy quickly crumbled. Many residents&nbsp;
concluded that Jones was not the messiah after all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:40.440
and saw the delegation as an opportunity&nbsp;
to escape. But when Jones’ more fanatical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:44.100
followers got wind of what was happening,&nbsp;
one of them lost his shit and tried to stab&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:49.320
the Congressman. Unsurprisingly the delegation&nbsp;
decided it was time to get the hell out of there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:52.080
taking fifteen congregation members with them.
 &nbsp;

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:57.120
But after hightailing it to a small airstrip&nbsp;
a few miles outside of Jonestown they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:02.160
intercepted by Jones’ personal militia. Armed&nbsp;
men stormed the runway with all guns blazing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:07.920
and by the time the bullets stopped&nbsp;
flying Ryan and 4 of his team were dead.
 &nbsp;

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:15.540
Horrific though that was, far worse was&nbsp;
about to take place back in Jonestown.
 &nbsp;

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:21.780
Jones knew that even by his own outlandish&nbsp;
standards, this was it; you can’t gun down a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:26.520
politician and expect to be left to play God in&nbsp;
the Jungle. There would be no quiet relocation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:33.420
this time. The US authorities would come after him&nbsp;
like a seagull after a bag of chips. So he took a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:38.760
drastic measure. Something that’s still hard to&nbsp;
hear about even today, almost 50 years later.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:44.040
He rounded up his most trusted lieutenants&nbsp;
and had them prepare a huge vat of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:49.560
soft drink flavor-aid, lacing it with a&nbsp;
cocktail of drugs. Jones knew he’d lost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:53.400
but if he was going down, he was&nbsp;
going to take everyone else with him.

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:59.700
Just in case you’re still on the fence about&nbsp;
what kind of guy Jim Jones was (I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:05.280
you probably aren’t - but just in case), I can&nbsp;
tell you he decreed that the congregation’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:10.200
children should be the first to drink the&nbsp;
poison. Jones’ own wife Marceline stepped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:15.420
in at this point in an attempt to stop the&nbsp;
madness, but guards held her back. As the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:21.540
children began to die with their parents watching&nbsp;
on, Marceline managed to break free, but it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:27.240
already too late. Distraught, she grabbed&nbsp;
a cup of poison and was dead minutes later.

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:34.740
In Jones’ own words, it was a ‘revolutionary&nbsp;
suicide’ - a protest against the evils of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:39.960
world. For many members of the People’s&nbsp;
Temple it wasn’t even suicide, let alone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:45.540
revolutionary. Jones had done his brainwashing&nbsp;
well - the few survivors claimed that most sat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:53.340
patiently waiting for their turn to die, but a&nbsp;
small minority refused to drink. Never one to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:59.640
no for an answer, Jones had his goons pin them&nbsp;
down and inject cyanide into their bloodstreams.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:09.480
In the space of just 45 minutes, a staggering 909&nbsp;
people were dead, 276 children among them. Jones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:15.240
was found with his followers, a bullet hole in his&nbsp;
head. Whether he committed suicide or was murdered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:21.600
by one of his flock, nobody knows for sure.&nbsp;
Either way, the People’s Temple was no more.
 
 &nbsp;

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:27.060
In the years since the massacre, there have&nbsp;
been many cult leaders who’ve preyed on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:32.640
good intentions and misguided faith of their&nbsp;
followers to line their own pockets and fulfil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:39.840
their own warped fantasies. But for sheer force&nbsp;
of personality, size of ambition and eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:45.600
scale of devastation, few have come close&nbsp;
to the sunglasses-wearing second-coming that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:51.960
was the Reverend Jim Jones. Thank God for that.
 
Thanks for watching. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 

